# Auto-restart kanata when a keyboard (re)connects, so it re-grabs the device.
# Fixes: MX KEYS B Bluetooth reconnect / suspend-resume dropping the grab
# (RUNBOOK Incident 4 / requirements OPS-3).
#
# CRITICAL: ATTRS{name}!="kanata" excludes kanata's OWN virtual keyboard —
# without it, kanata restarting would re-trigger this rule in an infinite loop.
#
# CRITICAL: the filename MUST sort after 60 — ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD is set by the
# input_id builtin in 60-input-id.rules. At priority 42 this rule evaluated
# before that property existed and silently never matched (RUNBOOK Incident 5).
#
# Uses SYSTEMD_WANTS -> oneshot kanata-regrab.service (not RUN+=systemctl):
# the burst of add-events from one reconnect coalesces into a single activation.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="1", ATTRS{name}!="kanata", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="kanata-regrab.service"
